    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>A3(A) <u>determine the slope of a line given</u> a table of values, <u>a graph</u>, two points on the line, <u>and an equation written in</u> various <u>form</u>s, including 
\(y = mx + b\), \(\underline{Ax + By = C}\), and \(y -y_1= m (x -x_1 )\)</entry>
      <entry>Partial coverage: Lesson provides content that covers part of this TEKS. The parts that are covered have been underlined.</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>A3(C) <u>graph linear functions on the coordinate plane</u> and identify key features, including  <u>\(x\)-intercept, \(y\)-intercept</u>, zeros, and <u>slope, in mathematical</u> and real-world <u>problems</u></entry>
    <entry>Partial coverage: Lesson provides content that covers part of this TEKS. The parts that are covered have been underlined.</entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</tgroup></table>
<title> Lesson Activities </title>
<para>Here are the instructional activities for the lesson:</para>
<list>
  <item> 1.11.1: Applying the Distributive Property to Rewrite Expressions  </item>
  <item>1.11.2: Relating Two-Variable Equations, Their Graphs, and Situations<list>
      <item>1.11.2: Self Check </item>
      <item>1.11.2: Additional Resources</item>
    </list>
  </item>
  <item>1.11.3:Reasoning Symbolically and Abstractly about Linear Equations<list>
      <item>1.11.3: Self Check </item>
      <item>1.11.3: Additional Resources</item>
    </list>
  </item>
  <item>1.11.4: Identifying the Features of a Graph</item>
</list>
<para>Students will also complete a series of problems in the 1.11.5: Practice.</para>
<title>Required Materials</title>
<para>none</para>
<title>Required Preparation</title>
<para>none</para>
<title>Lesson Vocabulary</title>
<para> During this lesson, it is important to: </para>
<list>
  <item>Familiarize students with the vocabulary words they will see throughout the lesson. Encourage students to look for
    these words and notice their use and meanings.</item>
  <item>Encourage students to use key vocabulary words in “math talk” and their written and oral explanations.
  </item>
  <item>Utilize a word wall. Sample cards are located here: <link url="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/8ed3aa68763498713b44d3c2e537ffe61b4755f0">Mathematics Vocabulary Word Wall Cards</link>.</item>
</list>
<para>Vocabulary words that are emphasized in this lesson include:</para>
